{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122534-archmaster-s-daimon","id":1122534,"title":"archmaster's daimon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T16:28:36-07:00","id":1122534,"title":"archmaster's daimon","content":"What becomes of a daimon when the character becomes an archmaster? It's one of the things IM really didn't cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:34:03-07:00","id":1122605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122534-archmaster-s-daimon#post1122534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What becomes of a daimon when the character becomes an archmaster? It's one of the things IM really didn't cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>It continues being a daimon?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T23:32:40-07:00","id":1122619,"title":"","content":"It is a part of their psyche. I don't see why it would change. That's probably why it wasn't mentioned in IM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T01:02:11-07:00","id":1122647,"title":"","content":"It would be really powerful, I think Dave mentioned Rank 6, so practically a deity. It's also worth considering that when a Mage joins a Prelacy and makes the given Exarch a part of himself and his agenda a part of his goals, 2E mentions that the Daimon is warped by the act. Now Archmasters have disproportionally big egos, big enough to say no to the Lie piercing nature of true knowledge the Paths offer, instead creating their own big ass road, where the ultimate goals are defined as very specific milestones set exclusively by them by burning them into their Cintamani, possibly running counter to other truths the Paths and other Archmasters espouse. It even permanently hurts their souls and decreases Gnosis when they ever try to change their Road's goals by fulfilling of which they intend to Ascend.<br /> <br /> Consider what I said above when describing the Daimon. The Daimon should probably be heavily subservient to the Archmage's goals yet also very powerful in its efforts to aid the Archmage to achieve them. Overall, highlight the aspect of cosmic arrogance. The contradicting nature of truths in various Cintamani and of the Paths and Cintamani might have been what led to the Fall and creation of the Abyss. After all, what is Abyss other than a bunch of contradicting Truths trying to affect reality at the same time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 07-30-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T03:29:00-07:00","id":1123384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122534-archmaster-s-daimon?p=1122647#post1122647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be really powerful, I think Dave mentioned Rank 6, so practically a deity. It's also worth considering that when a Mage joins a Prelacy and makes the given Exarch a part of himself and his agenda a part of his goals, 2E mentions that the Daimon is warped by the act. Now Archmasters have disproportionally big egos, big enough to say no to the Lie piercing nature of true knowledge the Paths offer, instead creating their own big ass road, where the ultimate goals are defined as very specific milestones set exclusively by them by burning them into their Cintamani, possibly running counter to other truths the Paths and other Archmasters espouse. It even permanently hurts their souls and decreases Gnosis when they ever try to change their Road's goals by fulfilling of which they intend to Ascend.<br /> <br /> Consider what I said above when describing the Daimon. The Daimon should probably be heavily subservient to the Archmage's goals yet also very powerful in its efforts to aid the Archmage to achieve them. Overall, highlight the aspect of cosmic arrogance. The contradicting nature of truths in various Cintamani and of the Paths and Cintamani might have been what led to the Fall and creation of the Abyss. After all, what is Abyss other than a bunch of contradicting Truths trying to affect reality at the same time...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Alternate Abyssal theory: the Abyss is the remnants of the fallen in the war for the Supernal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}